const BU_GENESIS_SCENE_ALT=Object.freeze({"g07-d01":"Wide ancient hill-country pasture shared by two growing households; sheep, cattle, tents, and separate herding groups; no required water source.","g07-d02":"Abram and Lot speaking amid tents; distant bifurcated landscape and packed goods; still illustration with three accessible hotspots.","g07-d03":"From a ridge: lush distant river plain versus stonier upland, with Lot and pack animals at a viewpoint.","g07-d04":"Single ultra-wide landscape still with Abram surveying land; Mamre/altar revealed by zoomable region or a gentle overlay, not a physically impossible 360° camera.","g07-d05":"Aftermath beyond a distant ancient city: Lot escorted with others; bundles being carried away; no fighting gore.","g07-d06":"Cinematic non-graphic scene of a rescued group returning; foreground Abram and Lot reunited, subdued dusty backdrop; separate progress-marker thumbnails are UI overlays, not invented events in one image.","g07-d07":"Respectful quiet meeting with bread and wine; Abram and priest-king distinguishable, modest ancient garments.","g07-d08":"King of Sodom with visible goods; Abram declines while allies stand nearby; no celebratory treasure-taking.","g07-d09":"Quiet night outside Abram’s tents, Abram gazing at a vast starry sky; one fixed illustrated frame with tap-able sky regions.","g07-d10":"Respectful, non-sensational still of pregnant Hagar resting alone at a wilderness spring; later birth conveyed by narrative UI rather than merging two moments into one photorealistic image.","g08-d01":"Abraham and Sarah at tent courtyard with quiet reverent atmosphere; name-pair tiles as UI only; no fabricated covenant relic.","g08-d02":"Abraham and three male-looking guests under broad trees; basin, bread and meal, no wings, no grand palace.","g08-d03":"Exterior tent scene with Sarah visible discreetly near the entrance, guests and Abraham in middle distance; zoom reveal supported.","g08-d04":"Abraham thoughtfully regarding distant city in late day; the numeric sequence appears as an accessible in-game overlay, not carved historical markers.","g08-d05":"Family moving away from distant walled city at sunrise, guided by men/angels with no wings; Zoar shown distantly; wife’s outcome narrated rather than sensationalized.","g08-d06":"Tender dignified scene outside family tent with elderly Sarah and infant Isaac; Abraham nearby; no gratuitous background family members.","g08-d07":"Respectful still at wilderness well: distressed Hagar and a youth-aged Ishmael, empty waterskin and water source; earlier family disagreement told through a narrated opening rather than two events in one illustration.","g08-d08":"Abraham and Isaac on rocky trail continuing ahead; donkey and two servants in midground; bundle of split wood clearly visible.","g08-d09":"Dignified aftermath just after intervention: Abraham and unharmed Isaac standing, ram visible among thorns; no weapon near Isaac.","g08-d10":"Abraham and Isaac returning through the hills in soft morning light; timeline/motif cards are interface components, not literal people from future nations gathered together.","g09-d01":"Aging Abraham respectfully briefing senior servant by tent beside prepared travel goods; Sarah’s passing is a narrated transition, not an invented family keepsake or living cameo.","g09-d02":"Ten clearly separated camels in a line in broad daylight, with servant and well-packed supplies; frame may zoom for counting.","g09-d03":"Evening setting: kneeling camels by ancient well, servant beside them, clay jar and long trough.","g09-d04":"Rebekah by well in motion, large camel trough, waiting camels and servant observing; water transfer animations as UI highlights over single still.","g09-d05":"Rebekah and servant by well with visible ring, pair of bracelets, travel bags, and distant doorway to family home.","g09-d06":"Welcoming courtyard with Rebekah, Laban, servant and camels; earlier well and route represented by accessible UI sequence.","g09-d07":"Servant seated with Rebekah’s household listening; four event-card UI overlays reference earlier episodes, no composite fantasy still.","g09-d08":"Rebekah calmly addressing her family in ancient courtyard; servant standing respectfully; emotional tone courageous rather than coerced.","g09-d09":"Wide sunlit departing camel caravan with women and servant in historically inspired clothes; household in distance.","g09-d10":"Late-day field with Isaac, camel caravan approaching, Rebekah with veil visible; gentle sunset mood, no modern wedding ceremony."});
